# .mailmap — canonical display names for this repository's history.
#
# A mailmap changes how Git (and GitHub) *display* authorship: it never rewrites
# a commit, a tag, a release or a SHA. Use it when the goal is that every commit
# shows the project owner's name without invalidating the published 0.9.1 tag and
# its CI-validated provenance.
#
# To actually rewrite the objects, use tools/rewrite_authors.sh, which applies
# this same mapping to a branch (and therefore changes every SHA it touches).
#
# Syntax:  Canonical Name <canonical@email>  Old Name <old@email>

# Automated tooling commits during the Qt6 port, attributed to the project owner.
Johan Polsinelli <83455892+jojo8356@users.noreply.github.com> <agent@arena.invalid>

# Same address, but recorded as the account login in older commits: a mailmap
# entry keyed only on the address would leave the name untouched, so the pair is
# spelled out here.
